cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Forecasting Wi-Fi channel occupancy from AERPAW spectrum recordings, including under simulated sparse monitoring"
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/awiecz/spectrum-occupancy-forecasting"
url: "https://github.com/awiecz/spectrum-occupancy-forecasting"
abstract: >-
  A deep dive into one public radio dataset (AERPAW fixed spectrum monitors, February 2022).
  It asks how well recent measurements, and models trained on them, forecast the busy fraction
  of a Wi-Fi channel 15 minutes ahead, and what happens when measurements are missing or late.
  All results are exploratory; the one independent test (the CC2 recording) has not been run.
